  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Cooperation between farmers and pastoralists over management of natural resources and access to basic social services enhanced.
- Shared and sustainable livelihood opportunities for different ethnic groups created. 
- Social and economic interaction between different ethnic groups  enhanced.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">- 0%
- 0%
- 0%</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">2021-2022 Targets:

Output 1: Community-based conflict resolution and reconciliation mechanisms are in use and working effectively to resolve conflict:
- Formation of 7 new Community-based Reconciliation mechanisms (CBRMs) in 7 communities.
- Training of 7 community peace committees.

Output 2: Peace dividends for community interdependence and co-existence delivered:
- Agric extension services for women groups
- Youth Group farming
- Income generation activities for women
- Establish 4 Village Saving and Lending Associations (VSLAs)
- Environmental and livelihood initiatives
- Demarcation of 20 km secondary migratory routes
- Rehabilitate Six handpumps to improve securely accessible safe drinking water sources.
- Construction of 2 market shelters in Kurti

Output 3: Women&#xb4;s organizations, including those representing pastoralist women, empowered to meaningfully participate in local and State-level peacebuilding platforms:
- Support 3 existing women CSOs in Geneina locality
- Construction women house in two communities</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022; 7 CBRMs established (213 members).</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
